{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared parity case table for the first-valid-wins pre-scenario arbiter.",
    "",
    "There are two implementations of one rule set: gui/scenario-arbiter.js (the",
    "browser host, issue #755) and src/lobby/scenario_arbiter.rs (the native host,",
    "issue #1326, written as a transcription of the JS rather than a second",
    "design). Nothing but prose held them together until this file: each side had",
    "its own hand-written cases, so a rule could drift on one side and every test",
    "would stay green. This table is consumed by BOTH:",
    "",
    "  * tests/client/scenario-arbiter-parity.test.js  (vitest, drives the JS)",
    "  * src/lobby/scenario_arbiter.rs `mod tests`     (cargo, drives the Rust)",
    "",
    "Add a case here, not to either consumer. A behaviour only one side can",
    "satisfy is a bug in that side, not a reason to fork the table.",
    "",
    "`outcome` is the JS's own outcome string, lowercased: accepted | ignored |",
    "rejected. `selection` is the selection the call RETURNS — which on ignored",
    "and rejected is the held one, normalised, never a half-write.",
    "",
    "Note (recorded rather than fixed): ServerMessage::ScenarioCatalog carries no",
    "`active_packs` field, so a native host's catalogue message cannot state the",
    "mod packs a browser host's synthesized one does. It is inert today — a native",
    "host applies no packs — so this is a note for slice #1328, not a gap the",
    "table can pin."
  ],
  "catalog": [
